# 15. Step 10 — Read Bronze

```python
bronze_df = spark.table("orders_bronze")
```

===================================================================================================

# 16. Step 11 — Remove duplicates

```python
silver_df = bronze_df.dropDuplicates(["order_id"])
```

Why?

Suppose the source has:

```text
ORD0001
ORD0001
ORD0002
```

We don't want two records for the same order.

After:

```text
ORD0001
ORD0002
```

===================================================================================================

# 17. Step 12 — Convert order date

```python
from pyspark.sql.functions import col

silver_df = silver_df.withColumn(
    "order_date",
    col("order_date").cast("date")
)
```

Now:

```text
"2026-03-04"
```

becomes a proper:

```text
DATE
```

===================================================================================================

# 18. Step 13 — Validate quantity

```python
silver_df = silver_df.filter(
    col("quantity") > 0
)
```

This removes invalid records such as:

```text
quantity = 0
quantity = -2
```

===================================================================================================

# 19. Step 14 — Validate price

```python
silver_df = silver_df.filter(
    col("unit_price") > 0
)
```

This prevents invalid prices:

```text
0
-500
```

