# 27. Step 21 — Gold: Sales by Product

```python
gold_product_sales = silver_df.groupBy("product").agg(
    sum("quantity").alias("total_quantity"),
    sum("total_amount").alias("total_sales"),
    count("order_id").alias("total_orders")
)

display(gold_product_sales)
```

Output:

```text
product       total_quantity    total_sales    total_orders
------------------------------------------------------------
Laptop        XX                XXXXXXX        XX
Mobile        XX                XXXXXXX        XX
Monitor       XX                XXXXXXX        XX
Mouse         XX                XXXXXXX        XX
...
```

Save it:

```python
gold_product_sales.write \
    .format("delta") \
    .mode("overwrite") \
    .saveAsTable("sales_gold_by_product")
```

===================================================================================================

# 28. Step 22 — Top 10 Customers

Requirement:

> Find customers who spent the most money.

```python
from pyspark.sql.functions import sum

top_customers = silver_df.groupBy(
    "customer_id",
    "customer_name"
).agg(
    sum("total_amount").alias("total_spent")
).orderBy(
    col("total_spent").desc()
).limit(10)

display(top_customers)
```

===================================================================================================

# 29. Step 23 — Save Top Customers

```python
top_customers.write \
    .format("delta") \
    .mode("overwrite") \
    .saveAsTable("sales_gold_top_customers")
```

Now we have another Gold table.

