# 32. SQL reporting

Once the Gold tables exist, you can use SQL.

### Total revenue

```sql
SELECT
    SUM(total_amount) AS total_revenue
FROM orders_silver;
```

### Total orders

```sql
SELECT
    COUNT(*) AS total_orders
FROM orders_silver;
```

### Completed orders

```sql
SELECT
    COUNT(*) AS completed_orders
FROM orders_silver
WHERE status = 'Completed';
```

### Cancelled orders

```sql
SELECT
    COUNT(*) AS cancelled_orders
FROM orders_silver
WHERE status = 'Cancelled';
```

### Sales by city

```sql
SELECT *
FROM sales_gold_by_city
ORDER BY total_sales DESC;
```

### Sales by product

```sql
SELECT *
FROM sales_gold_by_product
ORDER BY total_sales DESC;
```

### Top customers

```sql
SELECT *
FROM sales_gold_top_customers
ORDER BY total_spent DESC;
```

